      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "In the 5.5 to 7.0 $\\text{pH}$ range, the solubility of micronutrients like iron ($\\text{Fe}$) and manganese ($\\text{Mn}$) is generally favorable for grapevines. As soil $\\text{pH}$ rises beyond 7.0, these metals become less soluble and more prone to precipitation as hydroxides, making them less available for root uptake. This slightly acidic to neutral range optimizes the balance where enough of these essential nutrients remain soluble in the soil water for efficient foliar and root absorption.",
